Vendored third-party sources, unmodified.

crypt_blowfish 1.3
  Solar Designer <solar at openwall.com>, https://www.openwall.com/crypt/
  Public domain (see the notice at the top of each file).
  Files: crypt_blowfish.c/.h, crypt_gensalt.c/.h, wrapper.c, ow-crypt.h, crypt.h

  x86.S from the upstream tarball is intentionally NOT vendored: it is the x86
  assembly implementation of BF_body, and this sample must build the portable C
  one for arm64-v8a so the translator sees real ARM64 Blowfish code.

The libbcrypt wrapper one directory up (../bcrypt.c, ../bcrypt.h) is by
Ricardo Garcia <r@rg3.name>, dedicated to the public domain under CC0. It
expects crypt_blowfish to sit in a "crypt_blowfish" subdirectory, which is why
this layout is preserved verbatim.

Do not edit these files. If a translator bug appears to require a change here,
fix it in frameworks/libs/binary_translation/ instead -- the point of vendoring
the real library is that the sample runs the same code a shipping app does.
